## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design per-tenant policy enforcement, guard-detection, and prompt rewriting with auditable provenance.

## Key Concepts

- Multi-tenant policy registry and per-tenant constraints
- Guard-detection vs. prompt rewriting
- System guard injection and explicit privacy constraints
- Audit artifacts and drift/telemetry considerations

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal prototype sketch
const policy = {
  Tesla: { pii: true, retentionDays: 90 },
  Google: { pii: false, retentionDays: 365 },
  Plaid: { pii: true, retentionDays: 30 }
};
function guardAndRewrite(tenant, prompt) {
  const violations = [];
  const lower = prompt.toLowerCase();
  if (lower.includes("password") || lower.includes("ssn")) {
    violations.push("PII-like content");
  }
  const rewritten = `[${tenant}] ${prompt} /* guard: ensure policy compliance */`;
  return { rewritten, violations };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you evaluate determinism and drift for two tenants under evolving policies?  
- What tests would you add to catch policy-evading prompts without compromising latency?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to architect provenance-aware prompt pipelines at scale, ensuring data lineage, watermarking, and auditability across tenants with realistic latency constraints.

## Key Concepts

- Data provenance and lineage in LLM prompts
- Per-tenant guards, watermarking, policy enforcement
- Output verification with source citations via a mock knowledge graph
- Structured audit logging: input hash, rewritten prompt, per-model outputs, latency, drift verdict
- Security considerations around prompt leakage and PII

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal prototype sketch
function rewriteWithProvenance(prompt, tenantPolicy) {
  const provenance = `Source=${tenantPolicy.allowedSources.join('|')};Tenant=${tenantPolicy.id}`;
  return `${prompt}\n\n[Provenance:${provenance}]`;
}
function verifyOutput(output, sources) {
  const hasCitation = sources.some(s => output.includes(s));
  return hasCitation;
}
```

